<title>CHILE: Home Depot, Falabella link at $15 mln.</title>
<headline>Home Depot, Falabella link at $15 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Home Depot Inc's new subsidiary in Chile will have an initial capital investment of $15 million to be placed over three years, its local partner S.A.C.I. Falabella said Thursday.</p>
<p>Falabella will have a 33.33 share in the new company, The Home Depot Chile SA, said Falabella in a statement filed with the Chilean stock superintendency.</p>
<p>Home Depot's headquarters in Atlanta announced earlier that it formalized a joint venture with Falabella, Chile's top department store chain, to open Home Depot's first store outside North America. The new Chilean store was on target to open in 1998, it said.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
